{
  "dom_id": "step-q57187",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "$4÷\\frac{5}{7}=$",
  "worked_solution": "Dividing a whole number by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying the whole number by the reciprocal of the fraction.\n\nFirst, we write $4$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n4=\\frac{4}{1}\n$$\n\nNext, we note that the reciprocal of $\\frac{5}{7}$ is $\\frac{7}{5}.$ \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n4÷\\frac{5}{7}=\\frac{4}{1}÷\\frac{5}{7}=\\frac{4}{1}\\times \\frac{7}{5}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply our fractions. \n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{1}\\times \\frac{7}{5}=\\frac{4\\times 7}{1\\times 5}=\\frac{28}{5}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{28}{5}=5\\,\\text{R}3=5\\,\\frac{3}{5}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
